to your fathers in peace and be buried at a ripe old age.","from":8},{"book":"GEN","chapter":35,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":12,"source":"openbible","text":"And Isaac lived 180 years.","from":8},{"book":"GEN","chapter":35,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":12,"source":"both","text":"Then he breathed his last and died and was gathered to his people, old and full of years. And his sons Esau and Jacob buried him.","from":8},{"book":"1CH","chapter":29,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":12,"source":"both","text":"He died at a ripe old age, full of years, riches, and honor, and his son Solomon reigned in his place.","from":8},{"book":"GEN","chapter":49,"verse":33,"verseEnd":33,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"When Jacob had finished instructing his sons, he pulled his feet into the bed and breathed his last, and he was gathered to his people.","from":8},{"book":"JOB","chapter":42,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"And so Job died, old and full of years.","from":8},{"book":"GEN","chapter":25,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"Ishmael lived a total of 137 years. Then he breathed his last and died, and was gathered to his people.","from":8},{"book":"GEN","chapter":47,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":10,"source":"openbible","text":"“How many years have you lived?” Pharaoh asked.","from":8}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":4}]},"12-18":{"people":[{"id":"ishmael-h3458g","name":"Ishmael","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Abraham","count":4,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"abraham-h0085","name":"Abraham","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Terah","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"hagar-h1904","name":"Hagar","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"sarah-h8283","name":"Sarah","kind":"person","brief":"Sister of Abraham","count":1,"firstVerse":12},{"id":"adbeel-h0110","name":"Adbeel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Ishmael","count":1,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"kedar-h6938","name":