"inPassage":3,"uses":864},{"base":"H0085","lemma":"אַבְרָהָם","tr":"av·ra·ham","gloss":"Abraham","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":175},{"base":"H0110","lemma":"אַדְבְּאֵל","tr":"ad·be·el","gloss":"Adbeel","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H2301","lemma":"חֲדַד","tr":"cha·dad","gloss":"Hadad","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H4854","lemma":"מַשָּׂא","tr":"mas·sa","gloss":"Massa","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H6929","lemma":"קֵ֑דְמָה","tr":"qe·de·mah","gloss":"Kedemah","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":16,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"He will be a wild donkey of a man, and his hand will be against everyone, and everyoneʼs hand against him; he will live in hostility toward all his brothers.”","from":18},{"book":"GEN","chapter":17,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"As for Ishmael, I have heard you, and I will surely bless him; I will make him fruitful and multiply him greatly. He will become the father of twelve rulers, and I will make him into a great nation.","from":16},{"book":"GEN","chapter":20,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Now Abraham journeyed from there to the region of the Negev and settled between Kadesh and Shur. While he was staying in Gerar,","from":18},{"book":"1CH","chapter":1,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"These are their genealogies: Nebaioth the firstborn of Ishmael, then Kedar, Adbeel, Mibsam,","from":13},{"book":"1CH","chapter":1,"verse":31,"verseEnd":31,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"Jetur, Naphish, and Kedemah. These were the sons of Ishmael.","from":13},{"book":"PSA","chapter":83,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"the tents of Edom and the Ishmaelites, of Moab and the Hagrites,","from":12},{"book":"GEN","chapter":2,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The name of the first river is Pishon; it winds through the whole land of Havilah, where there is gold.","from":18},{"book":"GEN","chapter":10,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The sons of Cush: Seba, Havilah, Sabtah, Raamah, and Sabteca. And the sons of Raamah: Sheba and Dedan.","from":18}],"notes":[{"id":"gen-16-ishmael-nation","title":"Ishmael: twelve princes and a great nation","kind":"prophecy"}],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":4}]},"19-26":{"people":[{"id":"isaac-h3327","name":"Isaac","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Abraham","count":4,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"abraham-h0085","name":"Abraham","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Terah","count":1,"firstVerse":19},{"id":"rebekah-h7259","name":"Rebekah","kind":"person","brief":"Sister of Laban","count":2,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"bethuel-h1328a","name":"Bethuel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Nahor","count":1,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"laban-h3837a","name":"Laban","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Bethuel","count":1,"firstVerse":20},{"id":"esau-h6215g","name":"Esau","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":2,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":26}],"places":[{"id":"paddan-h6307","name":"Paddan","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":20}],"words":[{"base":"H3327","lemma":"יִצְחָק","tr":"yits·chaq","gloss":"Isaac","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":108},{"base":"H3816","lemma":"לְאֹם","tr":"le·om","gloss":"people","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":31},{"base":"H0761","lemma":"אֲרַמִּי","tr":"a·ram·mi","gloss":"Aramean","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":11},{"base":"H6279","lemma":"עָתַר","tr":"a·tar","gloss":"to pray","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":20},{"base":"H7259","lemma":"רִבְקָה","tr":"riv·qah","gloss":"Rebekah","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":30},{"base":"H3205","lemma":"יָלַד","tr":"ya·lad","gloss":"to beget","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":496},{"base":"H0990","lemma":"בֶּ֫טֶן","tr":"be·ten","gloss":"belly: abdomen","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":72},{"base":"H0802","lemma":"אִשָּׁה","tr":"ish·shah","gloss":"woman","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":781},{"base":"H6215","lemma":"עֵשָׂו","tr":"e·sav","gloss":"Esau","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":97},{"base":"H0085","lemma":"אַבְרָהָם","tr":"av·ra·ham","gloss":"Abraham","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":175}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"EZR","chapter":8,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":13,"source":"both","text":"So we fasted and petitioned our God about this, and He granted our request.","from":21},{"book":"GEN","chapter":27,"verse":40,"verseEnd":40,"votes":12,"source":"both","text":"You shall live by the sword and serve your brother. But when you rebel, you will tear his yoke from your neck.”","from":23},{"book":"2CH","chapter":33,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":12,"source":"both","text":"And when he prayed to Him, the LORD received his plea and heard his petition. So He brought him back to Jerusalem and to his kingdom. Then Manasseh knew that the LORD is God.","from":21},{"book":"ISA","chapter":58,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":12,"source":"both","text":"Then you will call, and the LORD will answer; you will cry out, and He will say, ‘Here I am.’ If you remove the yoke from your midst, the pointing of the finger and malicious talk,","from":21},{"book":"LUK","chapter":1,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":12,"source":"both","text":"But the angel said to him, “Do not be afraid, Zechariah, because your prayer has been heard. Your wife Elizabeth will bear you a son, and you are to give him the name John.","from":21},{"book":"GEN","chapter":27,"verse":29,"verseEnd":29,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"May peoples serve you and nations bow down to you. May you be the master of your brothers, and may the sons of your mother bow down to you. May those who curse you be cursed, and those who bless you be blessed.”","from":23},{"book":"1CH","chapter":5,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"And because they cried out to God in battle, they were helped against their enemies, and the Hagrites and all their allies were delivered into their hands. Because they put their trust in God, He answered their prayers.","from":21},{"book":"ROM","chapter":9,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":11,"source":"openbible","text":"Not only that, but Rebeccaʼs children were conceived by one man, our father Isaac.","from":21}],"notes":[{"id":"gen-25-23-older-serve","title":"Two nations in your womb","kind":"prophecy"}],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":6}]},"27-34":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":7,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"esau-h6215g","name":"Esau","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":6,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"isaac-h3327","name":"Isaac","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Abraham","count":1,"firstVerse":28},{"id":"rebekah-h7259","name":"Rebekah","kind":"person","brief":"Sister of Laban","count":1,"firstVerse":28}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H6215","lemma":"עֵשָׂו","tr":"e·sav","gloss":"Esau","lang":"h","inPassage":7,"uses":97},{"base":"H3290","lemma":"יַעֲקֹב","tr":"ya·a·qov","gloss":"Jacob","lang":"h","inPassage":8,"uses":350},{"base":"H1062","lemma":"בְּכֹרָה","tr":"be·kho·rah","gloss":"birthright","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":10,"top":true},{"base":"H5138","lemma":"נָזִיד","tr":"na·zid","gloss":"stew","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":6},{"base":"H0122","lemma":"אָדֹם","tr":"a·dom","gloss":"red","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":9},{"base":"H5889","lemma":"עָיֵף","tr":"a·yeph","gloss":"faint","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":17},{"base":"H6718","lemma":"צַ֫יִד","tr":"tsa·yid","gloss":"wild game","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":19},{"base":"H4376","lemma":"מָכַר","tr":"ma·khar","gloss":"to sell","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":80},{"base":"H9030","lemma":"נִי","tr":"ni","gloss":"me","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":908},{"base":"H7650","lemma":"שָׁבַע","tr":"sha·va","gloss":"to swear","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":186}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":21,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"And God was with the boy, and he grew up and settled in the wilderness and became a great archer.","from":27},{"book":"PRO","chapter":13,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"A righteous man eats to his heartʼs content, but the stomach of the wicked is empty.","from":29},{"book":"ISA","chapter":40,"verse":30,"verseEnd":30,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"Even youths grow tired and weary, and young men stumble and fall.","from":29},{"book":"ISA","chapter":40,"verse":31,"verseEnd":31,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"But those who wait upon the LORD will renew their strength; they will mount up with wings like eagles; they will run and not grow weary, they will walk and not faint.","from":29},{"book":"HEB","chapter":11,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"By faith he dwelt in the promised land as a stranger in a foreign country. He lived in tents, as did Isaac and Jacob, who were heirs with him of the same promise.","from":27},{"book":"HEB","chapter":12,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"See to it that no one is sexually immoral, or is godless like Esau, who for a single meal sold his birthright.","from":33},{"book":"HEB","chapter":12,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"See to it that no one is sexually immoral, or is godless like Esau, who for a single meal sold his birthright.","from":34},{"book":"HEB","chapter":12,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"For you know that afterward, when he wanted to inherit the blessing, he was rejected. He could find no ground for repentance, though he sought the blessing with tears.","from":34}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":4}]}}